---
title: Every feature
nav_title: Features
description: What a skyBlip Go does, one line each, and where each one is explained.
---

<section>
  <p class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-go", label: "skyBlip Go", class: "cta" %></p>
  <h1>Everything a skyBlip Go does.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    One line each, grouped by the page that explains it. Every name opens the paragraph behind it.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "radar", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Heading up", anchor: "heading-up" %></dt>
      <dd>You in the middle, nose up, and the sky turning around you: traffic to the upper right is off the right of the nose.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Rings of 1, 2, 4 or 8 NM", anchor: "heading-up" %></dt>
      <dd>Or 2, 4, 8 and 16 km, picked in the unit it is read in.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "A minute of track", anchor: "heading-up" %></dt>
      <dd>A line from each aircraft to where it will be in a minute, and your own two minutes ahead.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Every aircraft, however far", anchor: "every-aircraft" %></dt>
      <dd>PLOT ALL stands traffic past the ring on a band around it, on its bearing.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Every aircraft counted", anchor: "every-aircraft" %></dt>
      <dd>The figure in the corner is everything heard, placed or not.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Traffic advisory", anchor: "alarm" %></dt>
      <dd>Inside 3 km and 300 m, a quarter of the glass flashes towards the traffic, with sound, vibration and lamp.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Five shapes", anchor: "shapes" %></dt>
      <dd>Above, level or below, near or far in altitude, climbing or sinking, read without a legend.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "Nearby, nearest first", anchor: "nearby" %></dt>
      <dd>Callsign or address, ground distance and relative altitude, one row per aircraft.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "instruments", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "instruments", label: "Six-pack", anchor: "six-pack" %></dt>
      <dd>Ground speed, horizon, altimeter, turn and slip, track and vertical speed off the GNSS.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "instruments", label: "Battery on the glass", anchor: "six-pack" %></dt>
      <dd>The state of charge over the middle dial.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "instruments", label: "G-meter", anchor: "g-meter" %></dt>
      <dd>Normal, lateral and fore-and-aft load, with this flight's peaks.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "controls", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "controls", label: "Two contacts", anchor: "two-contacts" %></dt>
      <dd>The pad walks the pages, the button acts, and nothing needs timing.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "controls", label: "Settings on the device", anchor: "two-contacts" %></dt>
      <dd>Type, callsign, units, range, plot, alarm and volume, without a phone.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "controls", label: "Callsign field", anchor: "callsign" %></dt>
      <dd>A registration typed with two contacts, and cleared with one press.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "controls", label: "Diagnostics by name", anchor: "diagnostics" %></dt>
      <dd>Status, satellites, radio log, raw counters, capture and self test.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "power", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "power", label: "Says what it waits for", anchor: "waiting" %></dt>
      <dd>No fix, and how far the receiver has got.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "power", label: "Off is the wordmark", anchor: "off" %></dt>
      <dd>E-paper holds it with no power, and a blank glass is kept for storage.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "power", label: "A flat cell says so", anchor: "flat-battery" %></dt>
      <dd>The cutoff writes FLAT BATTERY before the rails drop.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "power", label: "A day on one cell", anchor: "cell" %></dt>
      <dd>A shutdown in order, and a radio that speaks once every ten seconds on the ground.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "power", label: "A gauge that holds still", anchor: "gauge" %></dt>
      <dd>Two curves, charging or not, and never moved by a transmit burst.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "phone", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "phone", label: "By name, no pairing", anchor: "by-name" %></dt>
      <dd>FLARM NMEA to three apps at once, over the profiles they look for.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "phone", label: "Asked on the glass", anchor: "asked" %></dt>
      <dd>Two presses allow, one refuses, and silence is a refusal.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "phone", label: "Firmware from a web page", anchor: "firmware" %></dt>
      <dd>A signed image over Bluetooth, and a device that goes back when the new one does not take.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "phone", label: "Why no pairing", anchor: "no-pairing" %></dt>
      <dd>The boundary is the signed image and the thumb on the device, not the link.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "radio", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radio", label: "Four dwells a second", anchor: "second" %></dt>
      <dd>Aligned on GPS to the microsecond, both 868 channels and the ground uplink.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radio", label: "Two systems in one dwell", anchor: "second" %></dt>
      <dd>ADS-L and FLARM-generation frames told apart after one sync.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "radio", label: "A burst nobody moves", anchor: "second" %></dt>
      <dd>About 5 ms, at an instant drawn from the address and the second.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "displays", class: "cta" %></h2>
  <dl class="catalog">
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "displays", label: "The radar, both ways", anchor: "both-ways" %></dt>
      <dd>The same skies with PLOT ALL and PLOT TO SCALE, one toggle apart.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "displays", label: "Every screen", anchor: "in-flight" %></dt>
      <dd>Every page, menu and prompt, as the firmware draws it.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><%= link_to_page "displays", label: "Why the screen behaves", anchor: "screen" %></dt>
      <dd>Partial refresh, a black wipe per page, and the full waveform twice a session.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <p>
    <%= link_to_page "radar", class: "cta cta--next" %>
    &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
